00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:42.000
And of course, it's been politicized, and that didn't help things. And I have lots of brilliant colleagues who could say much smarter things on this podcast about how to tackle that. That's not my specialty, but I do admire the great work being done in this field on the issues of polarization. And so what do we do from here? My team has spent a lot of time thinking in the last year and studying this problem and looking at different tactics from, we ran some, we call them mega studies, really, really massive randomized controlled trials where instead of testing a single hypothesis, we test literally dozens at the same time in parallel.

